---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";

// Registered as the privacy policy URL of the Meta app "GiveawayApp" (App ID 445937964421895).
// Keep the URL stable, and the page unlinked and noindex.
const lastUpdated = "October 16, 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | GiveawayApp"
  description="How GiveawayApp, a giveaway picker by Fjord Labs AB, handles creators' accounts and the comments people leave on giveaway posts."
  noindex={true}
>
  <section class="py-16 md:py-20 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold text-bark mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-bark/50">GiveawayApp</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-bark/40 mb-8">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="prose-article">
        <p>
          GiveawayApp (a working name) is a tool for picking giveaway winners. A creator runs a
          giveaway on their own post. GiveawayApp collects the entries, applies the creator's rules,
          draws the winners and makes a reveal video and a public proof page. It's made by
          Fjord Labs AB in Sweden, which is responsible for the data described here.
        </p>
        <p>
          This page covers two groups of people: <strong>creators</strong>, who use GiveawayApp to
          run a giveaway, and <strong>entrants</strong>, who commented on a giveaway post.
        </p>

        <h2>If you run a giveaway</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Your account:</strong> your email address and the identifier from the sign-in
            method you choose.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Your Instagram connection:</strong> when you click Connect Instagram, you log in
            on Instagram's own page and allow GiveawayApp to read your profile basics (username,
            account type, your posts) and the comments on your posts. We never see your password.
            Instagram gives us an access token, which we keep on our server and use only to import
            the comments of the posts you choose.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Your giveaways:</strong> what you enter, such as the title, prize, deadline,
            rules, logo and colours.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Payments:</strong> if you buy credits, Stripe handles the payment. We never see
            your card number; we keep a record of what you bought.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          GiveawayApp only reads. It never posts, replies, likes, hides or deletes anything on your
          account. It doesn't read your direct messages, your followers or who liked your posts.
        </p>

        <h2>If you commented on a giveaway</h2>
        <p>
          When a creator imports their giveaway post, we receive each comment's
          <strong>username, text and time</strong>, including replies. Nothing else from your
          profile. We use it only to run that giveaway: to check the creator's entry rules (for
          example, tagging friends), to count one entry per person and to draw the winners.
        </p>
        <p>
          So that anyone can check the draw was fair, the giveaway's proof page lists the entries
          for <strong>90 days</strong>. After that, we keep only the winners, the number of entries
          and a fingerprint (hash) of the list, which can't be turned back into names.
        </p>
        <p>
          The creator runs the giveaway and is responsible for it: the rules, the prize and
          contacting the winners. GiveawayApp is the tool they use.
        </p>

        <h2>What we never do</h2>
        <p>
          We don't sell data, show ads or use anyone's data for anything other than running
          giveaways. We don't use it to train AI models.
        </p>

        <h2>Services we use</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Meta (Instagram):</strong> the official Instagram API, to import comments.</li>
          <li><strong>Supabase:</strong> our database and sign-in.</li>
          <li><strong>Our web host:</strong> serves the pages, with standard server logs such as IP addresses.</li>
          <li><strong>Stripe:</strong> payments.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Some of these companies are based in the US. They process data only to provide their
          service to us, under the safeguards the GDPR requires, such as the EU Standard
          Contractual Clauses.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Full entry lists: 90 days after the draw, then only winners, counts and the hash.</li>
          <li>Instagram access token: until you disconnect, delete your account, or the token expires (after 60 days).</li>
          <li>Your account and giveaways: until you delete them.</li>
          <li>Payment records: 7 years, as Swedish bookkeeping law requires.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="delete">How to delete your data</h2>
        <p><strong>Creators:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            To stop our access to Instagram: in Instagram, go to Settings → Apps and websites and
            remove GiveawayApp. The access token stops working straight away.
          </li>
          <li>
            To delete what we hold: delete the giveaway or your account in GiveawayApp, or email us.
            We delete your giveaways, the imported comments and your token within 30 days, except
            the payment records the law requires us to keep.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>Entrants:</strong> email us your username and a link to the giveaway post. We'll
          remove your comment from that giveaway's stored entries and proof page within 30 days.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Under the GDPR you can ask what data we hold about you, and ask us to correct, delete or
          export it, or object to how we use it. Write to
          <a href="mailto:fjordlabs.app@gmail.com">fjordlabs.app@gmail.com</a>. You can also
          complain to the Swedish Authority for Privacy Protection (IMY).
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          When this policy changes, we update the date at the top. For important changes, we tell
          creators by email first.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
